      "side": 0,
      "message": "I added a comment [0] in yorp\u0027s board file where I make all of the changes that support V0 of the board. Since the GPIO_EN_USB_A1_5V (GPIO96) signal maps to EN_BRD_ID circuitry on V0, we don\u0027t have to worry about it asserting. Common code uses these usb_port_enable signal to turn on in S3+ and turn off in S5- (And also toggle by host or console command). For V0 board, the port 0 signal will still control both ports like it does today and the port 1 signal will have no effect (there isn\u0027t a feedback loop that will break either).\n\n\n[0] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/1087815/2/board/yorp/board.c#329",
